        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "54dee400-4ad7-578e-97b2-c6bf0071c772",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Bowie, Mick Ronson, Mick Woodmansey\n- Songs: \"Memory of a Free Festival\", \"The Man Who Sold the World\"\n- Albums: The Man Who Sold the World\n- Topics: studio debut, band line-up, release dates\n\nFacts:\n- A rock-oriented rendition of \"Memory of a Free Festival\" marked Mick Ronson's and Mick Woodmansey's studio debut with David Bowie's band.\n- The line-up assembled on \"Memory of a Free Festival\" would shortly record the album The Man Who Sold the World.\n- \"The Man Who Sold the World\" is a song written and performed by David Bowie.\n- \"The Man Who Sold the World\" is the title track of David Bowie's third album The Man Who Sold the World.\n- David Bowie's album The Man Who Sold the World was released in the US in November 1970.\n- David Bowie's album The Man Who Sold the World was released in the UK in April 1971.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
